  "root_cause": "The expression operator templates use dynamic_cast to classify lvalue root effects even when T already has a public, unambiguous LValueOperatorNode base. GCC correctly reports that this upcast can never be null. The runtime query is still necessary for other T values, including a most-derived layout with a separate lvalue subobject.",
  "fix": "Use if constexpr with std::is_convertible_v<const T*, const LValueOperatorNode*> to return true for the known upcast case. Preserve the pointer dynamic_cast and explicit null comparison otherwise. Apply consistently to all four templates. No ABI, field layout, compiler flag, public behavior or suppression change.",
